{"id":"mus-101-final","course":"MUS 101","kind":"final","title":"Final Exam","questions":[{"id":"f-q1","prompt":"Andreyev says music theory is best understood as:","choices":["A A laboratory physics theorem.","B A body of past practices (not a scientific theorem).","C A ban on historical styles.","D Only DAW automation rules."],"answer":1,"cite":"1.7","explain":"Not a scientific theorem—past practices continuing today."},{"id":"f-q2","prompt":"Music-theory knowledge in this course is framed as:","choices":["A Strict creative commandments.","B Descriptive grammar/syntax of what has been done.","C Marketing copy for streaming apps.","D Percussion-only tablature."],"answer":1,"cite":"1.8","explain":"Descriptive, not prescriptive."},{"id":"f-q3","prompt":"Two hallmarks of the Western tradition he stresses are:","choices":["A Purely oral monophony.","B Notation (writing music down) and polyphony.","C No clefs and no rhythm.","D Only microtonal continuum with no staff."],"answer":1,"cite":"1.11","explain":"Written tradition + polyphonic emphasis."},{"id":"f-q4","prompt":"Staff height encodes pitch by:","choices":["A Top = low; bottom = high.","B Bottom = lower sound; top = higher sound.","C Color of the ink only.","D Number of beams only."],"answer":1,"cite":"1.25","explain":"Spatial metaphor for pitch."},{"id":"f-q5","prompt":"Treble-staff spaces mnemonic he learned is:","choices":["A EGBDF.","B FACE.","C ACEG.","D GBDFA."],"answer":1,"cite":"1.43","explain":"F-A-C-E for spaces."},{"id":"f-q6","prompt":"Proportional/mensural notation chiefly gives:","choices":["A Absolute millisecond timings alone.","B Ratios/proportions among durations.","C Only lyrics.","D Timbre labels."],"answer":1,"cite":"2.3","explain":"Proportions between values."},{"id":"f-q7","prompt":"4/4 means:","choices":["A Three half notes per bar.","B Quarter-note beat; four quarters per bar.","C Eight whole notes.","D No meter."],"answer":1,"cite":"2.21","explain":"Four quarter notes per measure."},{"id":"f-q8","prompt":"In 4/4 accent hierarchy, the downbeat is:","choices":["A Weakest.","B Strongest (beat 1).","C Equal to beat 4.","D Undefined."],"answer":1,"cite":"2.23","explain":"Beat 1 strongest."},{"id":"f-q9","prompt":"6/8 vs 3/4 grouping:","choices":["A Identical beams.","B 6/8: two×three; 3/4: three×two.","C 6/8 forbids eighths.","D 3/4 is compound only."],"answer":1,"cite":"2.37","explain":"Beaming reveals different pulse groups."},{"id":"f-q10","prompt":"5/4 and 7/4 are examples of:","choices":["A Only simple duple.","B Asymmetric meters (mixed groupings).","C Unmetered chant exclusively.","D Tempo markings."],"answer":0,"cite":"2.31","explain":"Asymmetric meters combining groupings."},{"id":"f-q11","prompt":"A sharp before a note:","choices":["A Lowers a semitone.","B Raises a semitone (flat lowers; natural cancels).","C Doubles duration.","D Changes clef."],"answer":1,"cite":"3.11","explain":"Accidental definitions."},{"id":"f-q12","prompt":"Harmonic intervals are:","choices":["A Sequential only.","B Simultaneous tones.","C Rests only.","D Clefs."],"answer":1,"cite":"3.21","explain":"Simultaneous = harmonic."},{"id":"f-q13","prompt":"Major-scale pattern:","choices":["A S-T-T-S-T-T-T.","B T-T-S-T-T-T-S.","C All tones.","D All semitones."],"answer":1,"cite":"3.23","explain":"Tone–tone–semitone–tone–tone–tone–semitone."},{"id":"f-q14","prompt":"C major and A minor are relatives because they:","choices":["A Share no pitches.","B Share a key signature (white-key set in his demo).","C Share a tonic.","D Are identical scales."],"answer":1,"cite":"3.27","explain":"Same key signature."},{"id":"f-q15","prompt":"Perfect consonances named:","choices":["A Only thirds.","B Unison, 4th, 5th, octave.","C Only 7ths.","D Tritones."],"answer":1,"cite":"3.31","explain":"Perfect consonances list."},{"id":"f-q16","prompt":"“Key” names:","choices":["A Only dynamics.","B The tonic/central tone for stability and motion.","C Instrument brand.","D Page number."],"answer":1,"cite":"4.5","explain":"Central tone = tonic."},{"id":"f-q17","prompt":"Ascending fifths for major keys:","choices":["A Remove flats.","B Add sharps (F♯, C♯, G♯…).","C Delete key signatures.","D Add only double flats."],"answer":1,"cite":"4.13","explain":"Cycle of fifths adds sharps."},{"id":"f-q18","prompt":"A triad’s chord tones are:","choices":["A 2,4,6.","B Root, third, fifth (1,3,5).","C Only 1 and 8.","D Four stacked seconds."],"answer":1,"cite":"4.27","explain":"Triad = 1–3–5."},{"id":"f-q19","prompt":"Second inversion places which tone in the bass?","choices":["A Root.","B Fifth.","C Only the third.","D Leading tone always."],"answer":1,"cite":"4.31","explain":"Second inversion = fifth in bass."},{"id":"f-q20","prompt":"Functional stability order:","choices":["A Dominant > tonic > subdominant.","B Tonic most stable; subdominant mid; dominant unstable.","C All equal.","D Subdominant most stable."],"answer":1,"cite":"4.47","explain":"Tonic/subdominant/dominant stability."},{"id":"f-q21","prompt":"Dissonance, functionally, creates:","choices":["A Guaranteed beauty.","B Need for movement/resolution (vs stable consonance).","C Silence only.","D Faster tempo automatically."],"answer":1,"cite":"5.5","explain":"Stability vs need to move."},{"id":"f-q22","prompt":"String ratio 2:1 yields:","choices":["A Minor second.","B Octave.","C Tritone.","D Minor third."],"answer":1,"cite":"5.9","explain":"Half string → octave."},{"id":"f-q23","prompt":"Half cadence rests on:","choices":["A I after V–I.","B V as provisional goal.","C Only IV.","D VII."],"answer":1,"cite":"5.25","explain":"Imperfect/half cadence on V."},{"id":"f-q24","prompt":"Deceptive cadence:","choices":["A I–IV.","B V–VI.","C IV–I.","D II–V."],"answer":1,"cite":"5.29","explain":"V to VI."},{"id":"f-q25","prompt":"Plagal cadence:","choices":["A V–I.","B IV–I.","C VI–II.","D III–VI."],"answer":1,"cite":"5.33","explain":"IV to I."},{"id":"f-q26","prompt":"Quarter = 60 means:","choices":["A 60 measures per hour.","B 60 beats/minute (≈1 sec per beat).","C 60 sharps.","D 60 voices."],"answer":1,"cite":"6.13","explain":"BPM marking."},{"id":"f-q27","prompt":"Grace notes generally:","choices":["A Fill a full counted eighth in the meter math.","B Precede the main note and lack a definite counted value toward the bar.","C Replace clefs.","D Only appear in 5/4."],"answer":1,"cite":"6.22","explain":"Ornamental, not counted as ordinary eighth."},{"id":"f-q28","prompt":"Binary form is:","choices":["A Through-composed only.","B AB directional form.","C Twelve-tone only.","D Unmetered."],"answer":1,"cite":"6.37","explain":"AB form."},{"id":"f-q29","prompt":"Sonata exposition typically:","choices":["A Skips themes.","B Presents tonic theme, transitions (often to dominant), lays materials (often repeated).","C Is only a coda.","D Uses no harmony."],"answer":1,"cite":"6.61","explain":"Exposition layout."},{"id":"f-q30","prompt":"German ABA song forms aka:","choices":["A Only fugues.","B Lied forms.","C Tone rows.","D Isorhythm."],"answer":1,"cite":"6.55","explain":"Lied/Lieder."},{"id":"f-q31","prompt":"Core ear-training set includes:","choices":["A Only biography quizzes.","B Rhythmic/melodic/harmonic dictation and clapback.","C Only DAW editing.","D Conducting without sound."],"answer":1,"cite":"7.7","explain":"Four exercise types."},{"id":"f-q32","prompt":"Singing a dictation melody helps because:","choices":["A It erases memory.","B Retention and accurate writing improve; inner hearing matters.","C Notation becomes illegal.","D Pitch disappears."],"answer":1,"cite":"7.27","explain":"Sing to retain/write."},{"id":"f-q33","prompt":"Tritone mnemonic cited:","choices":["A Für Elise opening only.","B Simpsons theme’s first two notes.","C Happy Birthday.","D National anthems only."],"answer":1,"cite":"7.39","explain":"Simpsons = tritone aid."},{"id":"f-q34","prompt":"Listening vs hearing:","choices":["A Same thing.","B Hearing = physiology; listening = culture/intention/understanding.","C Listening ignores meaning.","D Hearing requires theory degrees."],"answer":1,"cite":"7.53","explain":"Culture vs mere sensation."},{"id":"f-q35","prompt":"6/8 feel to internalize:","choices":["A Six equal accents.","B Two groups of three eighths.","C One undivided pulse only.","D Strict 3/4 beams."],"answer":1,"cite":"7.57","explain":"Compound duple grouping."},{"id":"f-q36","prompt":"Bach chorales help you:","choices":["A Avoid polyphony.","B Hear four voices and practice harmony/voice-leading analysis.","C Skip cadences.","D Use only octaves."],"answer":1,"cite":"8.13","explain":"Four independent lines."},{"id":"f-q37","prompt":"D→G bass in G minor phrase-end ≈:","choices":["A Plagal only.","B Perfect cadence V–I.","C No cadence.","D Half cadence on IV."],"answer":1,"cite":"8.31","explain":"V–I perfect cadence."},{"id":"f-q38","prompt":"Picardy third means:","choices":["A Major piece ends minor.","B Minor piece ends with major tonic third.","C Only raised 4th.","D Triple meter."],"answer":1,"cite":"8.37","explain":"Minor→major close."},{"id":"f-q39","prompt":"First chorale-harmonizing step:","choices":["A Full orchestra sketch.","B Isolate soprano/hymn line; identify cadences.","C Inner voices before key.","D Ignore phrases."],"answer":1,"cite":"8.61","explain":"Cadences first."},{"id":"f-q40","prompt":"First approach to new music:","choices":["A Instant like/dislike.","B Curious, judgment-suspended listening across hearings.","C Genre loyalty only.","D Read spoilers only."],"answer":1,"cite":"8.49","explain":"Dispassionate interest first."}]}